Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: fsl_sai: constrain the Streamer to stereo during probing

The one-data-line Streamer card accepts two-channel streams.
ALSA test_channels nevertheless advertises wider formats, so a core
can select eight channels and then fail hw_params indefinitely.
Publish the board-specific stereo constraint in startup.

--- a/sound/soc/fsl/fsl_sai.c
+++ b/sound/soc/fsl/fsl_sai.c
@@ -895,6 +895,16 @@
 	struct fsl_sai *sai = snd_soc_dai_get_drvdata(cpu_dai);
 	bool tx = substream->stream == SNDRV_PCM_STREAM_PLAYBACK;
 	int ret;
+
+	/* The Streamer has one stereo data line. Advertise its actual channel
+	 * limit during probing, not only when hw_params rejects a wider stream.
+	 */
+	if (of_machine_is_compatible("fsl,imx7d-teufel-streamer")) {
+		ret = snd_pcm_hw_constraint_minmax(substream->runtime,
+				SNDRV_PCM_HW_PARAM_CHANNELS, 2, 2);
+		if (ret)
+			return ret;
+	}
 
